<title>AUSTRALIA: SWIMMING-AUSTRALIAN QUARTET BREAK MEDLEY WORLD RECORD.</title>
<headline>SWIMMING-AUSTRALIAN QUARTET BREAK MEDLEY WORLD RECORD.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australians Adrian Radley, Ryan Mitchell, Geoff Huegill and Michael Klim clocked a world short-course record three minutes 30.91 for the 4x100 metres medley relay on Sunday.</p>
<p>The previous best mark of 3:32.57 was set by an American quartet in 1993.</p>
